1038
01:39:29,198 --> 01:39:30,689
So what is Zestand?

1039
01:39:31,342 --> 01:39:34,884
Well, Zestand is a small state management library.

1040
01:39:35,310 --> 01:39:44,132
You can think of it as a place to keep app state that many components need to share, without passing props everywhere or writing Redux style boilerplate.

1041
01:39:44,398 --> 01:39:57,988
And async storage is a local persistent key value storage, which saves small pieces of data on the device like settings, cached app state, flags, or any non-sensitive session data.

1042
01:39:58,542 --> 01:40:00,384
So the idea here is simple.

1043
01:40:00,686 --> 01:40:08,544
Zestand manages the app state in memory, and async storage persists that state locally on the device.

1044
01:40:08,910 --> 01:40:14,020
So when you open up the app again after closing, the values still stay there.

1045
01:40:14,542 --> 01:40:23,716
Many companies like WhatsApp make use of async storage to store majority of data locally on your device, and you're learning how to do just that today.

1046
01:40:24,224 --> 01:40:32,516
So once the user selects a specific language, we can then store it locally and then restore it automatically whenever the app opens again.

1047
01:40:33,166 --> 01:40:38,180
